# Docs & Meta — consolidated release log

> Reorganized 2026-11-26 under DOCS-RELEASES-TOPIC-REORG-1 (#2974).
> Running history of docs & meta changes across
> releases; versions are sections, newest first. Section bodies are
> verbatim from the pre-reorg tree except markdown link targets,
> which were rewritten for the new paths (git history preserves
> the old layout).

## v0.26.0

### SCEN-DOCS-1

- Scenario docs pass: stale chain ids (`ait-mainnet`/`ait-hub`/
  `ait-devnet`/`ait-testnet`) corrected to `bc-2`; retired
  `messaging send --recipient`/`messaging topic` calls rewritten to the
  current `send --wallet --message [--topic]`/`topics` interface;
  `gpu list` → `gpu list-gpus`; `python -m json.tool` → `python3`.
  Scenario 08 (removed `market bid` group) retired to
  `docs/archive/scenarios`; README count corrected 58 → 51.


### DOCS-CMD-PARSE-1 (#559)

- `6a1102bf9`, `775d04e24` — new test extracts every `aitbc` command
  line from the scenario docs and resolves it with click's parser
  (parse only — no invocation, no CliRunner); 1,598 command lines
  checked, unparseable lines and bogus global-flag lines now fail the
  suite. `node info --node-id` doc line fixed.
- `c3e95c432` — `_resolve` walk split to satisfy the C901 ratchet.


## v0.25.13

### OPTION-DOCS-1

- docs(scenarios): option-level CLI coverage census lands as scripts/dev/gen_option_coverage.py (reads the staging SCENARIO-PLAY-1 census + cli-tree dump, emits the per-option exercise report). The census fix masking <placeholder> tokens before the shell-operator split revealed only 5 truly undocumented required options; docs gained a worked 'aitbc market host' example (scenario 11) and 'aitbc wallet bridge deposit/withdraw' entry-point lines (scenario 59). Required-but-undocumented options: 0. Refs #450


## v0.25.12

### docs(release): relocate post-tag entries from the v0.25.9 log to v0.25.11

- `f35a3df1` — the v0.25.9 tag froze its log, but 30 `### ` sections and a
  283-line commit index (2026-10-14/15 work, all inside the v0.25.11
  window) had been appended to it afterwards. They move to
  `v0.25.11_change.log`: sections appended in order, the hash list under a
  new `### Commit index` section so the coverage check still resolves
  every hash. `v0.25.9_change.log` matches its tag again except the
  retained internal-host-token scrub.


## v0.25.9

### docs(contracts): strip drifted helper lists from Python-contract stubs (2026-09-30)

The `docs/contracts/*` per-file stubs enumerate private helpers that have
drifted (`htlc.md` cited helpers removed from `htlc_contract.py`). The
"Key Functions" sections are removed; the class-level summaries verified
against the sources and each page carries a stub banner.


### docs(license): copyright year range 2025–2026 (2026-09-30)

`LICENSE` and the root `README.md` footer now read `Copyright (c)
2025–2026 AITBC` — the project spans both years.


### docs(cleanup): delete foreign 2025-dated templates; fix broken examples (2026-09-30)

Deleted foreign-template docs that describe a stack AITBC does not have:
`ci-cd/CI-CD-Pipeline-Guide.md` (Next.js/yarn/Stripe — self-labelled
foreign), and the `docs/database/` RLS set (PostgreSQL + Prisma + RLS;
nothing named `withUserContext`, `CREATE POLICY`, or `RLS_*` exists in
code): `RLS_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md`, `RLS_DATABASE_MIGRATION_SOP.md`,
`RLS_POLICY_CATALOG.md`, `DATA_DICTIONARY.md`. The two index READMEs were
part of the same import and are rewritten to point at the real schema doc
and the real CI files. `docs/security/SECURITY.md` reporting now defers
to `.github/SECURITY.md` (the actual policy). Fixed the broken imports a
reader would hit first: `aitbc.crypto.security` → `aitbc.crypto.secrets`,
`aitbc.security_hardening` → `aitbc.security.validators`,
`aitbc.redis_cache` → `aitbc.caching`, in `quick-start.md` and
`performance-features.md`. Dropped the stale per-app "last commit"
stamps from `architecture/active_apps.md`.


### docs(staleness): second sweep — SDK versioning, stale stamps, structure map (2026-09-30)

Follow-up on the stale-docs audit (Feb–Apr 2026 batch). `aitbc-agent-sdk`
is unpublished — install lines now show `pip install -e
packages/py/aitbc-agent-sdk`; doc versions ("v1.0.0") annotated against
the real package version (`0.1.0`); the "Planned v1.1.0 (2026-04-15)"
section reworded as unshipped candidates. Dropped the vestigial
"Generated: 2026-03-08" stamps from `blockchain/README.md` and
`reference/backend.md` (no generator runs). `REPOSITORY_STRUCTURE.md`
regained `aitbc/`, `mcp-server/`, `plugins/`, `skills/` and lost the
nonexistent `dev/` and `build/` rows.


### chore(docs): drop last baseline orphan — pytest_cache artifact (2026-09-30)

`.pytest_cache/` deleted (untracked pytest artifact; `.gitignore` already
covers it) and `orphan-docs-baseline.txt` is now empty — zero known
orphans. The checker learned to skip `#` comment lines so the baseline
can carry explanations.


### chore(docs): exempt tool-generated dirs in orphan check (2026-09-30)

`.pytest_cache/`, `.mypy_cache/`, `.ruff_cache/` and `node_modules/` are
now exempt prefixes in `check_orphan_docs.py` — pytest recreates
`.pytest_cache/README.md` on every test run, and a generated artifact
should never fail the orphan gate.


### feat(docs): mechanical evidence for ✅ feature-status rows (2026-09-30)

`check_feature_status.py` (new pre-commit hook
`validate-feature-status-evidence`) makes every `✅` in the feature
tables a verifiable claim: the row must carry a backticked code
identifier that resolves in the tree — otherwise it lands in
`feature-status-baseline.txt` (278 legacy rows baselined, ratchet only
shrinks). The bridge table in `2-bridge-cross-chain.md` is seeded with
real tokens (`BRIDGE_LOCK`, `refund_transfer`, `get_validator_set`, …);
its "Bridge Unlock" row now names the real on-chain type `BRIDGE_REFUND`,
and the threat-model row is `📄 doc` (a document, not shipped code).
Convention documented in `docs/meta/DOCUMENTATION_TEMPLATE_STANDARD.md`.


## v0.25.8

### 2026-09-28 — AGENTS.md is now cloner-facing

The repo `AGENTS.md` was rewritten from a 761-line operator workspace guide
into a ~125-line contributor/agent guide: repo layout, node deployment
entry points (`setup.sh`, `--open-island`), env-file and venv conventions,
development workflow (pre-commit, mypy/ruff/pytest, changelog tooling,
shell-script conventions), both contract test suites, and the MCP server.
All fleet-internal sections — gitea topology, sshfs, validator key layout
and rejoin runbook, faucet budgets, shell/SSH environment wiring, tea CLI —
moved to the operator's private workspace guide (`AGENTS/` detail files in
the IDE checkout). Fixes the always-on-rule injection truncating the file
mid-load.


